== 5.8 Chapter 5 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [The boundary between two drainage basins is the],
  [watershed],
  [confluence],
  [tributary],
  [flood plain]
)

#mcq(2, [A drainage basin is],
  [the area drained by a river and its tributaries],
  [the bed of a river only],
  [a lake on a flood plain],
  [the mouth of a river]
)

#mcq(3, [The point where a tributary joins the main river is a],
  [delta],
  [gorge],
  [source],
  [confluence]
)

#mcq(4, [The process by which water enters the soil is],
  [percolation],
  [infiltration],
  [runoff],
  [transpiration]
)

#mcq(5, [The downward movement of water through the soil into rock is],
  [evaporation],
  [infiltration],
  [percolation],
  [interception]
)

#mcq(6, [Water vapour leaving plants is called],
  [evaporation],
  [transpiration],
  [precipitation],
  [condensation]
)

#mcq(7, [The fastest route by which rainwater reaches a river is],
  [throughflow],
  [percolation],
  [groundwater flow],
  [surface runoff]
)

#mcq(8, [Which of these is NOT a process of river erosion?],
  [attrition],
  [abrasion],
  [deposition],
  [hydraulic action]
)

#mcq(9, [The process by which a river's load grinds its bed is],
  [hydraulic action],
  [attrition],
  [abrasion],
  [solution]
)

#mcq(10, [The wearing down of pebbles by collision with one another is],
  [saltation],
  [abrasion],
  [attrition],
  [solution]
)

#mcq(11, [The transport of fine silt in suspension gives a river its],
  [brown colour],
  [blue colour],
  [salinity],
  [speed]
)

#mcq(12, [Large stones rolled along a river bed are transported by],
  [saltation],
  [traction],
  [suspension],
  [solution]
)

#mcq(13, [Pebbles bounced along the bed are moved by],
  [solution],
  [suspension],
  [traction],
  [saltation]
)

#mcq(14, [A V-shaped valley is characteristic of the],
  [lower course],
  [middle course],
  [upper course],
  [delta]
)

#mcq(15, [Waterfalls are most common in the],
  [upper course],
  [delta],
  [lower course],
  [flood plain]
)

#mcq(16, [A waterfall forms where],
  [two rivers meet],
  [a river enters the sea],
  [the river deposits its load],
  [a band of hard rock overlies softer rock]
)

#mcq(17, [Interlocking spurs are formed by],
  [glacial erosion],
  [wave action],
  [lateral erosion in the upper course],
  [deposition on a flood plain]
)

#mcq(18, [Meanders are formed mainly by],
  [lateral erosion and deposition],
  [glacial plucking],
  [wind action],
  [vertical erosion]
)

#mcq(19, [An ox-bow lake is formed by],
  [a landslide blocking a river],
  [the cutting off of a meander loop],
  [the collapse of a limestone cave],
  [a lava flow damming a valley]
)

#mcq(20, [The outer bank of a meander is called the],
  [bluff],
  [delta],
  [slip-off slope],
  [levee]
)

#mcq(21, [A flood plain is formed mainly by],
  [wind deposition],
  [vertical erosion],
  [deposition during floods],
  [glacial deposition]
)

#mcq(22, [A levee is a],
  [ridge of glacial till],
  [sand dune],
  [natural embankment built by deposition at the river's edge],
  [wave-cut platform]
)

#mcq(23, [A delta forms where],
  [the river flows over a waterfall],
  [deposition exceeds removal at the mouth],
  [the sea erodes faster than the river deposits],
